    <sectiondef kind="func">
      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__vertex__functions_1ga16ac5393536b136d4c39dcfafaa64d21" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>const char</type>
        <definition>const char ndxlVertexHasNeighbour</definition>
        <argsstring>(NDXLVertex *_Source, NDXLVertex *_Destination)</argsstring>
        <name>ndxlVertexHasNeighbour</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1ad03a49b11a22416ba63273c4d7deb38b" kindref="member">NDXLVertex</ref> *</type>
          <declname>_Source</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1ad03a49b11a22416ba63273c4d7deb38b" kindref="member">NDXLVertex</ref> *</type>
          <declname>_Destination</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Checks if an edge exists between two vertices. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Source</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><computeroutput>Source</computeroutput> vertex (vertex 1 in edge creation).</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Destination</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><computeroutput>Destination</computeroutput> vertex (vertex 2 in edge creation).</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>If either _Source or _Destination are NULL, returns <ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gae9261a8e1c9a6cebdc947ee5798cca1e" kindref="member">NDXL_ERR</ref>, otherwise returns a bitmask detailing the coupling between _Source and _Destination:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>0, if no coupling exists</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>1 (bit 0), if at least one undirected coupling exists.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>3 (bits 0 and 1), if _Source has at least one directed edge to _Destination.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>5 (bits 0 and 2), if _Destination has at least one directed edge to _Source.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>7 (bits 0, 1, and 2) if at least one of each type of coupling exists between _Source and _Destination.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>This function runs in linear time proportional to ndxlGetVertexDegree(_Source). If ndxlGetVertexDegree(_Source) is larger than ndxlGetVertexDegree(_Destination), it may be worth swapping the arguments to reduce the traversal cost. However, doing so reverses the interpretation of the directed-edge flags.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Errors raised</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gaf6b8bdcb87bdd7944810152b510101e4" kindref="member">NDXL_ARG_ERR</ref> : _Source is NULL.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gaf6b8bdcb87bdd7944810152b510101e4" kindref="member">NDXL_ARG_ERR</ref> : _Destination is NULL.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="group__edge__creation_1ga64a610b6a899977bbf5722ca30f92114" kindref="member">ndxlCreateEdge</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
