      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__vertex__functions_1ga1f59cebd8575f89020b590ba036006c8" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>double *</type>
        <definition>double * ndxlVertexState</definition>
        <argsstring>(NDXLVertex *_Vertex)</argsstring>
        <name>ndxlVertexState</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1ad03a49b11a22416ba63273c4d7deb38b" kindref="member">NDXLVertex</ref> *</type>
          <declname>_Vertex</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Provides direct access to the internal state vector of a vertex. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Vertex</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Target vertex to see the state of.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>If _Vertex is NULL, returns NULL, otherwise returns a pointer to the internal state vector or, when called from within a dynamics function, the current Runge–Kutta stage vector of _Vertex.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>When called outside a dynamics function, this function returns a pointer to the vertex&apos;s primary state vector. When called from within a dynamics function, it instead returns a pointer to the current intermediate Runge–Kutta stage vector. This behaviour allows the same function to be used for directly modifying a vertex&apos;s state outside integration and accessing its current integration stage during dynamics evaluation.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="warning"><para>Direct modification of the returned vector is supported when it refers to the primary state vector. However, when called from within a dynamics function, the returned pointer refers to the intermediate Runge–Kutta stage vector. Modifying this vector directly is not intended for ordinary state updates and may interfere with the integration process.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Errors raised</title><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1gaf6b8bdcb87bdd7944810152b510101e4" kindref="member">NDXL_ARG_ERR</ref> : _Vertex is NULL.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="group__network__simulation" kindref="compound">Network Simulation</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
